SUMMARY:Wild Edibles Plant Walk
DESCRIPTION:Join TLC for a walk through Williamson's wild abundance!\nWe will explore our new edible plant walkway along with the variety of wild edible plants growing along two-ponds loop! Participants will leave with new knowledge of the identification\, history\, and uses of the many edible plants growing in the piedmont. This plant ramble will be about a mile\, moving at a slow pace through two ponds loop and surrounding areas. Please wear good walking shoes and bring a water bottle. This is a free event\, but preregistration is required:\n\n\nIf registration is full\, please email Meera Butalia at mbutalia@triangleland.org to be added to the waitlist.\nInclement Weather Policy: In the event of inclement weather\, you will be contacted by email for a call on cancellation or postponement.
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/wild-edibles-plant-walk
LOCATION:Williamson Farm and Nature Preserve\, 4429 Old Country Mial Rd\, Raleigh\, 27610\, United States
END:VEVENT
